# managed:start
# MANAGED by EpiAwarePackageTools.scaffold — do not edit by hand.
# Standard ignore rules live between the markers below and are
# replaced on every update. Add package-specific rules after the
# closing marker — they are preserved across updates.
# Julia: Manifest.toml records a resolved env. For a package (not an
# application) it must NOT be committed — a committed Manifest resolved on
# newest Julia fails the lts CI job, and its git-tree-sha1 hashes trip the
# detect-secrets pre-commit hook. Ignore it across every environment.
Manifest.toml
**/Manifest.toml
**/Manifest-*.toml

# Generated documentation output and dependencies.
docs/build/
docs/node_modules/
docs/package-lock.json
# README-derived and API-reference pages are generated by docs/make.jl.
docs/src/index.md
docs/src/lib/public.md
docs/src/lib/internals.md
# The release-notes page (from the repo's GitHub releases) and the
# Literate-rendered tutorial markdown are also generated by docs/make.jl.
docs/src/release-notes.md
docs/src/getting-started/tutorials/*.md
# The benchmark pages (performance-over-time + AD comparison, #299/#305):
# their own top-level nav folder, not under TUTORIALS_SUBDIR.
docs/src/benchmarks/*.md
# The performance-history page's Plots.jl chart (#114) is regenerated on
# every docs build and sits beside that page, so it moved with it (#299/#305).
docs/src/benchmarks/overall_trend.png

